    description: "VIOLATED (campaign 4 of WI-hagom, 2026-11-18). Four planted faults (framework_patterns.clear_pattern_cache 'drop call'; c._c_ambiguous_names 'drop call'; io_boundary.declared_by_an_included_header 'drop call'; ir.Edge.__post_init__ 'negate if') each failed packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_kept_work_guard.py::test_live_tree_is_clean, which select_by_statement left out. Each fails ALONE (-n 0) with its fault and passes without it. The test reads every source file as text (check-kept-work): it ran none of the changed statements, and its outcome depends on the text. smart-test's file-level manifest adds such readers (coverage-select readers, prose_only.tests_reading); the by-statement selector never consulted the read record.\n\nFIX (branch jgstern-agent/fix/statement-select-readers): select_by_statement adds every test recorded reading a changed file as data, for any kind of change, in the index's spelling (Selection.readers). Also: analyzer_identity._hash_package_py_files named hash-only for the recorder (median 1,012 readers per changed file before, against 345 tests kept by statement; nearly all from that hash).\n\nCLOSE CONDITION. On the live index, select_by_statement keeps the guard test for all four faults (bar/recheck_readers.py: done, CLEAN before merge); merged; after the next full run, the readers per changed file measured again with the hash-only read gone."  # 9378
    fields:  # 9378
      statement: "A test recorded reading a changed file as data is in the by-statement selection, whatever kind of change it is."  # 9378
      root_cause: "select_by_statement selected only from coverage records and never consulted the read record that the file-level manifest already uses."  # 9378
